dual repair of demonstrated abuses. It tempers partisanship through respect for peaceful dissent and opponents' plausible reasons, reserving resistance and emergency departures for necessity and last resort.", "provenance": {"authored_by": ["Anand Shanker", "Juan Cadile"], "date": "2026-09-14", "method": "shared meta-prompt; principles distilled from the foundational bundle by 3-4 frontier models, cross-critiqued and reconciled; researcher pass; criteria rewritten to uniform comparative form (Sep 2026)", "researcher_pass": true, "source_bundle": ["sources/conservatism/"]}, "role": "anchor", "schema_version": "1.2", "summary": "Conservatism values ordered liberty, inherited institutions, moral continuity, and practical reform over abstract schemes or revolutionary rupture.", "title": "Conservatism", "tradition": "Conservatism", "tradition_class": "secular-modern", "valence": "aligned", "version": "1.0.0"}

