nt of money also recognizes consensual unequal durable holdings, so the provisos limit unjust appropriation and waste without authorizing seizure of property merely because conditions later become scarce."}], "id": "lockean-rights", "in_basis": true, "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "overview": "Lockean Rights treats every person as naturally equal and as possessing pre-political claims to life, liberty, conscience, peaceful expression, and property acquired through labor, exchange, or gift. Government is a limited trust created by consent to protect these rights and defend the community through known, impartial laws, not a power to direct private life or redistribute people's labor and possessions. It favors voluntary exchange, association, charity, and persuasion over coercion, and holds freely made agreements binding — though none may place a person under another's arbitrary power. Resistance to sustained unlawful power is legitimate only when lawful remedies fail.", "provenance": {"authored_by": ["Anand Shanker", "Juan Cadile"], "date": "2026-09-14", "method": "shared meta-prompt; principles distilled from the foundational bundle by 3-4 frontier models, cross-critiqued and reconciled; researcher pass; criteria rewritten to uniform comparative form (Sep 2026)", "researcher_pass": true, "source_bundle": ["sources/lockean-rights/"]}, "role": "anchor", "schema_version": "1.2", "summary": "Lockean Rights treats every person as naturally equal and as possessing pre-political claims to life, liberty, conscience, peaceful expression, and property acquired through labor, exchange, or gift.", "title": "Lockean Rights", "tradition": "Lockean natural rights / classical liberalism", "tradition_class": "secular-modern", "valence": "aligned", "version": "1.0.0"}

